  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "All four red lines are respected: per-model failure rates go to purchasers and regulators but not the general public (NW-1/HC-1), the retrofit deadline is 6 years (NW-2), and suppression starts at 36 months (HC-2). S1 is only 'acceptable' because the residual reporting duty is limited to 'confirmed' incidents (serious-incident 24 h reporting and 72 h customer notice are safe). S2 keeps the 5% / 55 °C test but lets a regulator-approved corrective-action plan keep an above-limit model on the market with no stated time limit, and S5's mandatory 8-per-100k recall applies to Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) while sparing Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.4)."
